-No shirt, no shoes, no script.

2225
01:22:04,471 --> 01:22:06,093
-Okay, uh, "Hello, Muddah.

2226
01:22:06,128 --> 01:22:09,579
Hello, Faddah.
here I am at, uh, Catalina."

2227
01:22:09,614 --> 01:22:11,133
That's not it.
-Unh-unh, unh-unh.

2228
01:22:11,167 --> 01:22:12,306
-Ehh.

2229
01:22:12,341 --> 01:22:14,964
♪♪

2230
01:22:14,999 --> 01:22:16,828
-Mm-hmm.

2231
01:22:16,862 --> 01:22:17,933
Mm!

2232
01:22:17,967 --> 01:22:20,142
-Zack Norman as Sammy
in "Chief Zabu."

2233
01:22:20,176 --> 01:22:23,007
-Hm!

2234
01:22:23,041 --> 01:22:24,525
Uh-oh.

2235
01:22:24,560 --> 01:22:27,356
-It's the big guy.

2236
01:22:27,390 --> 01:22:31,222
♪♪

2237
01:22:31,256 --> 01:22:33,500
-I have to sit like this
since the implant.

2238
01:22:33,534 --> 01:22:35,674
♪♪

2239
01:22:35,709 --> 01:22:37,987
-I'm watching you, crayon head.

2240
01:22:38,022 --> 01:22:40,472
-Oi! Ouch! Oww!
-Ouch-ee! Oh, oh, hot!

2241
01:22:40,507 --> 01:22:41,646
Hot!
-Ooh, asphalt!

2242
01:22:41,680 --> 01:22:45,098
Oh! Ouch! Oh!
-[Panting]

2243
01:22:45,132 --> 01:22:47,824
-Any luck?
-Nothing.

2244
01:22:47,859 --> 01:22:49,481
Here come the bunnies.
Maybe they did better.

2245
01:22:49,516 --> 01:22:50,896
-Hoppin' down the bunny trail.

2246
01:22:50,931 --> 01:22:52,864
-Hey, it's Charlie's Angels,
plus a smart one!

2247
01:22:52,898 --> 01:22:54,900
-Nobody! At least,
not anybody who looks like

2248
01:22:54,935 --> 01:22:56,661
the two you fought with
on the Lira.

2249
01:22:56,695 --> 01:22:58,801
-Keep looking.
-Move out, troops!

2250
01:22:58,835 --> 01:23:00,803
-Oh, it's"McMillan & Wife & Wife & Wife."

2251
01:23:00,837 --> 01:23:02,598
-Can I talk to you a minute?

2252
01:23:02,632 --> 01:23:04,151
-What?
-Talk!

2253
01:23:04,186 --> 01:23:05,463
Just a minute.
-We gotta go.

2254
01:23:05,497 --> 01:23:06,671
What's wrong?
-Uh, I'm pregnant.

2255
01:23:06,705 --> 01:23:08,742
-About yesterday...

2256
01:23:08,776 --> 01:23:10,295
I'm sorry I slapped you.

2257
01:23:10,330 --> 01:23:11,987
And I wasn't really
drowning, either.

2258
01:23:12,021 --> 01:23:14,299
-Oh, yeah, and I'm not acting.
-I forgot all about that.

2259
01:23:14,334 --> 01:23:15,991
-Really?
-Really.

2260
01:23:16,025 --> 01:23:17,233
But you do pack
a pretty mean wallop.

2261
01:23:17,268 --> 01:23:18,510
-Oh, don't rub it in.

2262
01:23:18,545 --> 01:23:20,202
-I was gonna say,
"for a pretty girl."

2263
01:23:20,236 --> 01:23:22,100
-Ah, but you're ugly.

2264
01:23:22,135 --> 01:23:24,620
-Listen, Charlie Moss
has got a groovy sister.

2265
01:23:24,654 --> 01:23:26,104
And you know who else thinks so?

2266
01:23:26,139 --> 01:23:27,726
-The football team?

2267
01:23:27,761 --> 01:23:28,831
-Tad.

2268
01:23:28,865 --> 01:23:31,351
-Well, I apologized to him, too.

2269
01:23:31,385 --> 01:23:33,146
-Oh-whoa!
-Only first.

2270
01:23:33,180 --> 01:23:35,148
-Oh!
-It's them!

2271
01:23:35,182 --> 01:23:38,323
-[Gasps]

2272
01:23:38,358 --> 01:23:39,497
-Go find Charlie.

2273
01:23:39,531 --> 01:23:40,670
Quick.
-Right now!

2274
01:23:40,705 --> 01:23:42,224
-Hmm, hey, Charlie.

2275
01:23:42,258 --> 01:23:43,363
-I'll take him on.

2276
01:23:43,397 --> 01:23:44,536
I know I can.
I'll do it.

2277
01:23:44,571 --> 01:23:45,606
-Yeah!
- I will, I will, I will.

2278
01:23:45,641 --> 01:23:50,266
♪♪

2279
01:23:51,647 --> 01:23:55,099
♪♪

2280
01:23:55,133 --> 01:23:57,446
-Hm, hm, hm, hm, hm. Hm?

2281
01:23:57,480 --> 01:23:58,619
-Hm! Lucky!

2282
01:23:58,654 --> 01:23:59,965
Open table.

2283
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:04,970
♪♪

2284
01:24:05,005 --> 01:24:07,801
-Hmm.

2285
01:24:07,835 --> 01:24:10,286
-How come he got a menu already?

2286
01:24:10,321 --> 01:24:12,806
Lucky.

2287
01:24:12,840 --> 01:24:14,463
-Ugh! Peach daiquiri!

2288
01:24:14,497 --> 01:24:16,120
So, that's what
I drank last night.

2289
01:24:16,154 --> 01:24:17,604
Hm.

2290
01:24:17,638 --> 01:24:20,331
Tasted pretty good.
-Nice spit take, dude.

2291
01:24:22,988 --> 01:24:24,335
-We've got to get the scroll...

2292
01:24:24,369 --> 01:24:26,337
-I'm still waiting
for my spinach omelet.

2293
01:24:26,371 --> 01:24:28,925
-And no slip-up this time.

2294
01:24:32,481 --> 01:24:34,276
-Hi!
-Uh, yes, I am.

2295
01:24:34,310 --> 01:24:35,967
You?
-I've been looking for you.

2296
01:24:36,001 --> 01:24:37,279
-It's Creepy Girl!

2297
01:24:37,313 --> 01:24:39,833
-Don't make any heroic moves,
my friend.

2298
01:24:39,867 --> 01:24:41,662
-It's too late
to rewrite the script.

2299
01:24:41,697 --> 01:24:43,319
-Hand it over.

2300
01:24:43,354 --> 01:24:45,149
-Angelo!
What are you doing here?

2301
01:24:45,183 --> 01:24:47,151
-Working, being evil.
Shut up!

2302
01:24:47,185 --> 01:24:48,497
-I don't have time for games.

2303
01:24:48,531 --> 01:24:51,155
-And I haven't got time
for the pain.

2304
01:24:51,189 --> 01:24:53,191
-Angelo!
-Aw, man.

2305
01:24:53,226 --> 01:24:55,711
Everybody's coming
down on Angelo.

2306
01:24:55,745 --> 01:25:00,233
♪♪

2307
01:25:00,267 --> 01:25:02,200
-Thank you.

2308
01:25:02,235 --> 01:25:04,547
-Creep.

2309
01:25:04,582 --> 01:25:06,549
♪♪

2310
01:25:06,584 --> 01:25:07,723
-After him, teen gang!

2311
01:25:07,757 --> 01:25:08,896
-Yeah!

2312
01:25:08,931 --> 01:25:11,209
[Laughter]

2313
01:25:11,244 --> 01:25:13,384
-D'oh! Oof!

2314
01:25:13,418 --> 01:25:16,283
-When you're a Jet,
you're a Jet all the way.

2315
01:25:16,318 --> 01:25:17,733
-Splendid, son!

2316
01:25:17,767 --> 01:25:19,010
-It's a Catalina army knife.
-That's the Boy Scot motto.

2317
01:25:19,044 --> 01:25:20,529
Always be prepared.
-And effeminate.

2318
01:25:20,563 --> 01:25:23,877
-We'll take care of the garbage.Go get 'em, Don.

2319
01:25:23,911 --> 01:25:25,292
Can you handle this
for Mr. Duval?

2320
01:25:25,327 --> 01:25:28,985
-It's the land fuzz!
-Some call them land pigs.

2321
01:25:29,020 --> 01:25:32,299
-You bunnies stay here.
Duty calls your master away.

2322
01:25:32,334 --> 01:25:35,475
-Hm? What'd he mean by that?

2323
01:25:35,509 --> 01:25:37,649
Okay, people.
Everybody wear eye protection.

2324
01:25:37,684 --> 01:25:38,892
There's a lot of loose ends

2325
01:25:38,926 --> 01:25:40,928
flying together
all at once here.

2326
01:25:40,963 --> 01:25:42,689
-Wow,
this Main Street, U.S.A. parade

2327
01:25:42,723 --> 01:25:44,484
is really getting thin.

2328
01:25:44,518 --> 01:25:46,693
-[High-pitched] Hi, folks!
-That's not Mickey --

2329
01:25:46,727 --> 01:25:47,935
that's Nicky!

2330
01:25:47,970 --> 01:25:49,592
-Hey, he's running into
the Haunted Mansion.

2331
01:25:49,627 --> 01:25:51,042
-Oooh!

2332
01:25:52,008 --> 01:25:55,288
I'm your Ghost Host.

2333
01:25:55,322 --> 01:25:56,634
-Owie! Ouch!

2334
01:25:56,668 --> 01:25:58,187
-Oww! Oww! Ouch! Hot!
-Owie, owie, owie!

2335
01:25:58,222 --> 01:26:00,500
-Oh, ooh, ouch, hot, hot!

2336
01:26:00,534 --> 01:26:02,847
-D'oh. D'oh. D'oh. D'oh!

2337
01:26:02,881 --> 01:26:04,538
Pratfall, anyone?
Pratfall?

2338
01:26:04,573 --> 01:26:06,195
I got 'em all!

2339
01:26:06,230 --> 01:26:08,059
-Ouch, ouch, oww!
-Owie, ow, ooh!

2340
01:26:08,093 --> 01:26:09,612
It hurts!

2341
01:26:09,647 --> 01:26:12,028
-Hm, no exit through there.

2342
01:26:12,063 --> 01:26:12,995
-Hm.
-Alright.

2343
01:26:13,029 --> 01:26:15,480
Come on, come on!

2344
01:26:15,515 --> 01:26:16,964
-Hyah!

2345
01:26:16,999 --> 01:26:18,690
-Nice tag.

2346
01:26:18,725 --> 01:26:21,106
-D'oh, hey, lady!

2347
01:26:21,141 --> 01:26:22,763
-They put the skateboard
in the film!

2348
01:26:22,798 --> 01:26:25,076
-Well, wow!

2349
01:26:25,110 --> 01:26:26,802
Oh!
-Don't snag on me.

2350
01:26:26,836 --> 01:26:28,804
Don't snag on me!
-Eat it, boy.

2351
01:26:28,838 --> 01:26:31,807
Eat it.
-Oh!

2352
01:26:31,841 --> 01:26:33,153
-Oh, no. No.

2353
01:26:33,188 --> 01:26:34,948
-Look out, Mr. Ferguson!

2354
01:26:34,982 --> 01:26:37,502
-Jerry, no!
-I'm sorry, Mr. Ferguson!

2355
01:26:37,537 --> 01:26:40,091
-Oh, here it goes!
[All shouting]

2356
01:26:44,129 --> 01:26:46,822
-You got me all wet, boy.

2357
01:26:46,856 --> 01:26:49,031
-Well, guess he's swimming
back to Greece.

2358
01:26:49,065 --> 01:26:52,207
♪♪

2359
01:26:52,241 --> 01:26:54,036
-Little late, aren't you, buddy?

2360
01:26:54,070 --> 01:26:57,039
♪♪

2361
01:26:57,073 --> 01:26:58,351
-Take a rest, friend.

2362
01:26:58,385 --> 01:27:00,594
You've provided enough
comic relief.

2363
01:27:00,629 --> 01:27:02,320
Thank you,
Corky the water clown,

2364
01:27:02,355 --> 01:27:05,323
for making us laugh
at love...again.

2365
01:27:05,358 --> 01:27:06,945
-What do you think you're doing?

2366
01:27:06,980 --> 01:27:09,293
-I've got you this time, Duval.

2367
01:27:09,327 --> 01:27:11,467
-Will you take these
silly things off my wrist?

2368
01:27:11,502 --> 01:27:12,813
-I'm the silly thing!

2369
01:27:12,848 --> 01:27:14,159
-I've waited a long time
for you make a slip.

2370
01:27:14,194 --> 01:27:16,472
Now I've got you!
-What's this all about?

2371
01:27:16,507 --> 01:27:17,818
Who are you?

2372
01:27:17,853 --> 01:27:19,475
-Fingers O'Toole,
insurance investigator.

2373
01:27:19,510 --> 01:27:21,339
-FBI. Pratfall Division.
-This man is my prisoner.

2374
01:27:21,374 --> 01:27:24,515
-And what's the charge?
-Grand theft.

2375
01:27:24,549 --> 01:27:26,344
-And wearing an ascot.

2376
01:27:26,379 --> 01:27:28,795
-Look, you don't even know
what you're talking about.

2377
01:27:28,829 --> 01:27:30,969
-You stole the scroll
from the collection,

2378
01:27:31,004 --> 01:27:32,730
and it's in that case
you're holding.

2379
01:27:32,764 --> 01:27:35,905
-Oh, wow.
He's holding, dude.

2380
01:27:35,940 --> 01:27:37,459
-Hmm.

2381
01:27:40,324 --> 01:27:42,291
-Hey, cool!
A Bon Jovi poster.

2382
01:27:42,326 --> 01:27:43,810
-It's kind of like a peashooter,isn't it?

2383
01:27:43,844 --> 01:27:45,121
-Mm, a big one.

2384
01:27:45,156 --> 01:27:46,157
-It's gone!

2385
01:27:46,191 --> 01:27:47,641
-My career!
-It was in there.

2386
01:27:47,676 --> 01:27:50,299
I know it was in there!

2387
01:27:50,334 --> 01:27:52,301
-Why me?
Why me all the time?

2388
01:27:52,336 --> 01:27:55,477
-Where did it go?

2389
01:27:55,511 --> 01:27:56,995
-I don't believe it.

2390
01:27:57,030 --> 01:27:59,998
-I'm Iggy Pop.
-Oh, boy.

2391
01:28:00,033 --> 01:28:02,380
-Hey, the script's
in Braille now.

2392
01:28:05,176 --> 01:28:07,143
-He looks about 40.

2393
01:28:07,178 --> 01:28:08,524
-Closing time, young fella.

2394
01:28:08,559 --> 01:28:10,699
-The guy who lives here
wants to go to bed.

2395
01:28:10,733 --> 01:28:13,357
-Sure is beautiful.
-Yes, sure is.

2396
01:28:13,391 --> 01:28:16,877
♪♪

2397
01:28:16,912 --> 01:28:20,225
-Man, I sure love that
old snot-rag of a...

2398
01:28:20,260 --> 01:28:21,951
-Huh?!

2399
01:28:23,850 --> 01:28:26,473
[Whistle blows]

2400
01:28:26,508 --> 01:28:29,338
-So, you know, mi amor...
-The pain! The pain!

2401
01:28:29,373 --> 01:28:31,340
[All groaning]

2402
01:28:31,375 --> 01:28:32,168
Stealing art!

2403
01:28:32,203 --> 01:28:33,618
Win one, lose one --

2404
01:28:33,653 --> 01:28:35,448
famous American cliché.

2405
01:28:35,482 --> 01:28:37,139
-Shaving my head.

2406
01:28:37,173 --> 01:28:39,141
-I told you it would be
a long walk home.

2407
01:28:39,175 --> 01:28:40,970
-Didn't I tell you that?
-Enjoy?

2408
01:28:41,005 --> 01:28:43,801
-Oh, you promiscuous
manly robot monster.

2409
01:28:43,835 --> 01:28:45,872
-Kill him! Kill him!

2410
01:28:45,906 --> 01:28:49,047
-Musical newspaper from Japan.

2411
01:28:49,082 --> 01:28:50,532
And look!

2412
01:28:50,566 --> 01:28:52,534
Zack Norman as Sammy
in "Chief Zabu" --

2413
01:28:52,568 --> 01:28:54,881
it says it right there.

2414
01:28:54,915 --> 01:28:56,227
Oho!
-Oh, wow.

2415
01:28:56,261 --> 01:28:57,884
-Yikes!

2416
01:28:57,918 --> 01:29:04,062
♪♪

2417
01:29:04,097 --> 01:29:06,099
-Eh!

2418
01:29:06,133 --> 01:29:08,412
Let's quit.
I'm hemorrhaging.

2419
01:29:08,446 --> 01:29:10,414
-Hey, Mom, Dad,
you got any rhythm left?

2420
01:29:10,448 --> 01:29:11,415
We're out.
-How?

2421
01:29:11,449 --> 01:29:13,106
-How did it get out of my case,

2422
01:29:13,140 --> 01:29:15,211
back into the museum?
-Go figure.

2423
01:29:15,246 --> 01:29:17,938
-As Charles would say,
"Don't knock it, Dad."

2424
01:29:17,973 --> 01:29:20,113
Perhaps it's best forgotten,
anyway.

2425
01:29:20,147 --> 01:29:22,633
Lakopolous has
sailed away forever,

2426
01:29:22,667 --> 01:29:25,049
perhaps a little bit wiser
for his experience.

2427
01:29:25,083 --> 01:29:26,878
-I doubt it.
-There's only one answer, Anne.

2428
01:29:26,913 --> 01:29:28,915
Somebody up there likes us.

2429
01:29:28,949 --> 01:29:30,019
-No, dear.

2430
01:29:30,054 --> 01:29:32,297
I think someone loves us.

2431
01:29:32,332 --> 01:29:34,369
-Well, it's not me.

2432
01:29:34,403 --> 01:29:36,371
-Well, what now?

2433
01:29:36,405 --> 01:29:38,545
What's left for us?
-Drug running?

2434
01:29:38,580 --> 01:29:40,892
-Not one single prospect
on the entire island.

2435
01:29:40,927 --> 01:29:42,480
-Prostitution?
-I've searched high and low.

2436
01:29:42,515 --> 01:29:45,172
The pigeons have all flown away.-Slumlords?

2437
01:29:45,207 --> 01:29:47,174
-Well,
you could always go to work.

2438
01:29:47,209 --> 01:29:49,522
-Y-- Work?!
-Huh?!

2439
01:29:49,556 --> 01:29:51,386
-Oh.
-As Charles might say,

2440
01:29:51,420 --> 01:29:52,904
that's a boss idea.

2441
01:29:52,939 --> 01:29:56,391
You know,
it's time I did some retiring.

2442
01:29:56,425 --> 01:29:59,048
-Oh, there's that
Louis Nye look-alike contest.

2443
01:29:59,083 --> 01:30:01,050
We could dance goofy.

2444
01:30:01,085 --> 01:30:08,230
♪♪

2445
01:30:08,264 --> 01:30:10,543
-Ah, I've outgrown
this pratfall stuff.

2446
01:30:10,577 --> 01:30:11,751
It was just a phase.

2447
01:30:11,785 --> 01:30:13,511
Now I'm a swingin' cat!

2448
01:30:13,546 --> 01:30:14,547
Yeah!

2449
01:30:14,581 --> 01:30:16,238
-Hey, it's a skinhead!

2450
01:30:16,272 --> 01:30:18,758
Get Geraldo!
-[Chuckles]

2451
01:30:18,792 --> 01:30:20,276
-Say!

2452
01:30:20,311 --> 01:30:21,761
-Oh, look at Creepy Girl.

2453
01:30:21,795 --> 01:30:26,282
Doesn't she look great
in a hairdo like that?

2454
01:30:26,317 --> 01:30:27,767
I like her in a flip.

2455
01:30:27,801 --> 01:30:30,114
♪♪

2456
01:30:30,148 --> 01:30:32,288
-Oh, he's down to one girl, huh?He's cutting back.

2457
01:30:32,323 --> 01:30:35,947
Oh, nobody wants to dance
with the big stinky guy.

2458
01:30:35,982 --> 01:30:37,466
-Shirt's louder than the music,
isn't it?

2459
01:30:37,501 --> 01:30:40,469
-Yeah.

2460
01:30:40,504 --> 01:30:43,092
-Ahh, dork shack!
-Geek shack.

2461
01:30:43,127 --> 01:30:46,648
-Dork shack, baby, yeah!
-That's where it's at.

2462
01:30:46,682 --> 01:30:49,167
-Got a movie
that's as long as a whale.

2463
01:30:49,202 --> 01:30:51,998
-It's about to set sail!
Whoo!

2464
01:30:52,032 --> 01:30:54,000
-A plot hole
that's as big as a whale.

2465
01:30:54,034 --> 01:30:56,416
-Huzzah! King John invites
you to the Ren Festival.

2466
01:30:56,451 --> 01:30:59,350
Come see 300 years
crammed into one place.

2467
01:30:59,384 --> 01:31:01,386
Meet the people you snagged on
in high school.

2468
01:31:01,421 --> 01:31:04,148
Bring your own tights
or wear some of our own.

2469
01:31:04,182 --> 01:31:05,494
-Uh, principals to the front,
please.

2470
01:31:05,529 --> 01:31:07,013
Extras in back.
There you go.

2471
